<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.capture.resumes ~ capture mints the warm daemon lazily again

The hook-lever stands on its own: a marker file a capture hook checks and steps aside on when present (whatever runs the `lares sense capture` and `lares sense telemetry` legs on a session event). A migration or a `lares sense teardown` then runs WITHOUT daemon-spawn contention: the minting stops at the source, with no whack-a-mole against spawned children. `lares mempalace quiesce` pauses AND drains the warm daemons in one gesture; this lever suppresses minting alone, touching no live daemon.

`hooks resume` removes the marker and answers {wasPaused, hooksPaused, marker}; hooks already live answer an idempotent no-op.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ resume

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`resume` params=`~ un-pause the hooks`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ write

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`write` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ removes the marker file; idempotent, reversible by pause, trusted`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ resumed · already-live

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`resumed` params=`exit/0 fields/[[wasPaused hooksPaused marker]] ~ the marker stands removed; capture mints lazily again`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`already-live` params=`exit/0 ~ the hooks were already live; nothing to do`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

